# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Theta Desk
#
# Everything under data/ is either a secret, a cache, or a rebuildable
# artefact.  The database alone is ~250 MB of churning binary and holds the
# trade journal; the HTTP cache is another ~75 MB.  Both are reconstructed by
# `python pipeline.py`, so neither belongs in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets -- password hash, session signing key, generated plaintext
data/auth.json
data/auth.json.tmp
data/INITIAL_PASSWORD.txt
.env

# Personal settings: account size, risk appetite, your own watchlist.
# config.py imports this last, so it overrides the published defaults.
config_local.py

# Data, caches and logs (all rebuildable)
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
